68:   `@@SELFCHECK@@` token in the source; and the self-mutant lane (on its device mutant: a FAIL token and a FAIL line
69:   naming the geometry row).  **Gate 2 discards the exit status.**
70: * **The measurement's device variants** (the Opus seat's, reused): `dropold` (a drop-oldest ring: three COVERED
71:   `chk()` comparisons fail), `drqring` (the DRQ status bit dropped: two VERDICT-HANDED `chk()` rows fail), `w57hi`
72:   (word 57's high byte zeroed: four `row_cmp()` rows fail), each also with the self-mutant applied (`_sm`) for the lane;
73:   and `selfmut`, `cyl13`, `srstbit`, `rev255`, `w58lo`.
74: 
75: ## 3. THE CODE UNDER REVIEW (the generated #551f file, md5 7fd15d1d)
76: 
77: ### 3a. The two comparators, each with its (B) report
78: 
79: ```c
80: static void row_cmp(const char *why, uint64_t sectors, uint64_t got57, uint64_t got60)
81: {
82: 	rowcmp_calls ++;
83: 	rows ++;
84: 
85: 	if (got57 != sectors || got60 != sectors) {
86: 		printf("  FAIL %-38s sectors=%llu -> 57/58=%llu 60/61=%llu\n",
87: 		    why, (unsigned long long)sectors,
88: 		    (unsigned long long)got57, (unsigned long long)got60);
89: 		failures ++;
90: 		cmp_fails ++;
91: 		if (why[0] != '@')	/*  #551f: contract (B) -- a covered failure reports itself  */
92: 			printf("  FAIL  covered comparator failure -- %d failures so far\n", cmp_fails);
93: 	} else {
94: 		printf("  ok   %-38s %llu\n", why, (unsigned long long)sectors);
95: 	}
96: }
97: 
98: static void chk(const char *name, long long got, long long want)
99: {
100: 	chk_calls ++;
101: 	rows ++;
102: 	if (got != want) {
103: 		failures ++;
104: 		cmp_fails ++;
105: 		printf("  FAIL %-40s got %lld want %lld\n", name, got, want);
106: 		if (name[0] != '@')	/*  #551f: contract (B) -- a covered failure reports itself  */
107: 			printf("  FAIL  covered comparator failure -- %d failures so far\n", cmp_fails);
108: 	} else
109: 		printf("  ok   %-40s %lld\n", name, got);
110: }
111: ```
112: 
113: ### 3b. The block comment -- the contract, as the partition (A)-(D)
114: 
115: ```c
116: /*
117:  *  @@SELFCHECK@@ -- #551.  CAN THIS FILE'S COMPARATORS STILL FAIL?  Feeds chk() and row_cmp() known answers --
118:  *  each operand zero and past 32 bits, each of row_cmp()'s two disjuncts alone with got both below and
119:  *  above its want, and one probe per comparator that must NOT fail -- and requires the EXACT change in
120:  *  `failures' and in cmp_fails for each, restoring `rows', `failures' and cmp_fails after every probe.
121:  *  Run FIRST (before any row) and LAST (after every row, before the identity row), so a comparator that
122:  *  goes inert partway through is caught at one end or the other; the LAST run also requires the
123:  *  comparator call counts (chk() 24, row_cmp() 8).  Only the success arm prints gate 2's G text; see (D)
124:  *  for what the failure arms do.
125:  *
126:  *  WHAT IT COVERS: the rows that go through chk() and row_cmp() -- the last run prints how many calls
127:  *  each comparator took.  Of chk()'s calls, the ones in row_ring_occupancy_sound() that pass a
128:  *  `cond ? 1 : 0' (or `? 0 : 1') hand it a VERDICT computed at the call, not a comparison, and every
129:  *  other row in this file compares inline: neither is covered by this block.  "Covered" means the
130:  *  COMPARATOR is live, not that a row is.  The 8 verdict-handed calls still REPORT through (B): the file
131:  *  covers 24 comparisons and reports all 32 comparator failures.
132:  *
133:  *  WHAT THIS FILE'S CHECKS CAN AND CANNOT SEE.  Every check here reads state this file writes (the
134:  *  tallies, the call counts, `rows', sc_g) or output this file prints, so an edit that reproduces a healthy
135:  *  run's observables is invisible to all of them.  That boundary is a fact about in-file checks, not a gap
136:  *  in this block, and only a gate-side run on a device that fails a COVERED row sees across it (filed:
137:  *  `wdcidlane', on the FIRST covered row).  Inside the boundary:
138:  *
139:  *  (A) THE COMPARATORS ARE PINNED -- the probes require the exact change in `failures' and cmp_fails on
140:  *  their own calls, so an inert or narrowed comparator is caught at one end of the run or the other.  Not
141:  *  caught, measured: a test inside a comparator keyed on a value, a name, a position or this block's phase
142:  *  that the probes do not share; a predicate rewritten to agree with the original on every probe and differ
143:  *  elsewhere (the sum of the two gots against twice the want, say); and the code that FEEDS a comparator
144:  *  (row() handing row_cmp() its own want).
145:  *
146:  *  (B) A COVERED FAILURE REPORTS ITSELF -- on a non-probe mismatch each comparator prints a line gate 2's
147:  *  failure-count check reads (`N failures so far'), at the moment it fails; that check compares every such
148:  *  line in the log against "0", so a printed line cannot be taken back and no line can be added.  Hence no
149:  *  edit that leaves the covered rows running and the comparators intact hides a covered failure: not the
150:  *  trailer's count, token or exit rewritten singly or together, not a reset of either tally or both at any
151:  *  placement, not rows moved or deferred past the verdict with their counts forged (measured: #551f's
152:  *  pass, regress/artifacts/wdcidselfcheck_20260925/measured/run551f.out).  Not caught: that report switched off for
153:  *  non-probe calls -- its guard is itself a probe/real key -- together with an edit that hides the tallies.
154:  *
155:  *  (C) A ROW THAT DOES NOT RUN CANNOT REPORT -- the identity row's 128 and the LAST run's call counts
156:  *  (chk() 24, row_cmp() 8) raise the cost of skipping covered rows, and both are values this file can
157:  *  forge: skipping the ring rows while printing their gate-pinned labels and adding 24 to `rows' and
158:  *  chk_calls is one insertion and green here.  That is the boundary's own class; its close is `wdcidlane'.
159:  *
160:  *  (D) This block itself.  Nothing this block prints carries the self-mutant row's text, "high byte" or a
161:  *  pinned label.  Gate 2's G text is printed ONCE, by the last run, only when both runs passed; the run's
162:  *  PASS needs that line (sc_g) and both tallies at zero; a probe failure forces one failure, and a missing
163:  *  first run is counted by the trailer's `!sc_g' line.  Reviewed in the differential, not chased.  The rest
164:  *  of the file is filed as `wdcidcomparators' (#551; owner ruling 2026-09-25).
165:  */
166: ```
167: 
168: ### 3c. The self-check, with the call-count pin
169: 
170: ```c
171: static int sc_first_bad = -1;	/*  -1 until the FIRST run has happened  */
172: static int sc_g;	/*  set ONLY where gate 2's G line prints: the run's PASS needs it  */
173: 
174: static void selfcheck(const char *where)
175: {
176: 	static const long long cg[] = { 1, 0x100000000LL, 0, 0, 7 };
177: 	static const long long cw[] = { 2, 0, 1, 0x100000000LL, 7 };
178: 	static const uint64_t rw[] = { 2, 2, 1, 3, 0x100000000ULL, 0x100000000ULL, 0, 0 };
179: 	static const uint64_t r57[] = { 1, 2, 0, 3, 0, 0x100000000ULL, 1, 0 };
180: 	static const uint64_t r60[] = { 2, 1, 0, 3, 0x100000000ULL, 0, 0, 1 };
181: 	int sc_f = failures, sc_r = rows, sc_c = chk_calls, sc_rc = rowcmp_calls, sc_cf = cmp_fails, sc_bad = 0;
182: 	int i, n = 0;
183: 
184: 	for (i = 0; i < 5; i++, n++) {
185: 		chk("@@SELFCHECK@@/chk", cg[i], cw[i]);
186: 		if (failures != sc_f + (cg[i] != cw[i]) || cmp_fails != sc_cf + (cg[i] != cw[i]))
187: 			sc_bad++;
188: 		failures = sc_f; rows = sc_r; cmp_fails = sc_cf;
189: 	}
190: 	for (i = 0; i < 8; i++, n++) {
191: 		row_cmp("@@SELFCHECK@@/row", rw[i], r57[i], r60[i]);
192: 		if (failures != sc_f + (r57[i] != rw[i] || r60[i] != rw[i])
193: 		    || cmp_fails != sc_cf + (r57[i] != rw[i] || r60[i] != rw[i]))
194: 			sc_bad++;
195: 		failures = sc_f; rows = sc_r; cmp_fails = sc_cf;
196: 	}
197: 	chk_calls = sc_c; rowcmp_calls = sc_rc;
198: 	if (sc_bad) {
199: 		printf("  FAIL  SELFCHECK(%s): %d of %d probes answered wrongly\n", where, sc_bad, n);
200: 		failures = sc_f + 1; rows = sc_r; cmp_fails = sc_cf;
201: 	}
202: 	if (where[0] == 'f') {
203: 		sc_first_bad = sc_bad;
204: 		if (!sc_bad)
205: 			printf("  ok    SELFCHECK(first): all %d probes answered right\n", n);
206: 		return;
207: 	}
208: 	/*  #551e: a second identity constant -- the LAST run requires the comparator call counts the note line
209: 	    below prints, chk() 24 and row_cmp() 8.  It catches covered rows skipped or moved without their counts
210: 	    forged; like the identity row's 128 it is forgeable by an edit that writes the counter (contract (C)).
211: 	    Change these with the rows.  */
212: 	if (chk_calls != 24 || rowcmp_calls != 8) {
213: 		printf("  FAIL  SELFCHECK(last): chk() ran %d times and row_cmp() %d before this run; want 24 and 8\n",
214: 		    chk_calls, rowcmp_calls);
215: 		if (!sc_bad)
216: 			failures = sc_f + 1;
217: 		sc_bad++;
218: 	}
219: 	if (!sc_bad && sc_first_bad == 0) {
220: 		sc_g = 1;
221: 		printf("  ok    SELFCHECK the comparator can still fail (first and last)\n");
222: 	} else if (!sc_bad)
223: 		printf("  FAIL  SELFCHECK(last): the first run did not run, or did not pass\n");
224: 	printf("  note  SELFCHECK comparator calls this run: chk() %d, row_cmp() %d\n",
225: 	    chk_calls, rowcmp_calls);
226: }
227: ```
228: 
229: ### 3d. The identity row and the trailer
230: 
231: ```c
232: 	/*
233: 	 *  IDENTITY GUARD.  Two files with this name once differed only by the case of a
234: 	 *  parent directory, and the stale one encoded a REVERSED design decision.  A row
235: 	 *  count is the cheapest proof that the file which RAN is the file that was
236: 	 *  reviewed.  Last, so it counts every row above it.
237: 	 *
238: 	 *  It is also floor clause (c): against a null medium -- a stale copy, or a
239: 	 *  comment-only source -- this row is what refuses to report a pass.
240: 	 */
241: 	rows ++;
242: 	if (rows != 128) {
243: 		printf("  FAIL %-38s rows = %i, want 128\n",
244: 		    "[IDENTITY] row count", rows);
245: 		failures ++;
246: 	} else {
247: 		printf("  ok   %-38s %i\n", "[IDENTITY] row count", rows);
248: 	}
249: 
250: 	/*  #551: the PRINTED count shows the comparators' failures even after a reset of `failures' placed
251: 	    before this line (untouched, `failures' always counts at least as many); the verdict and the exit
252: 	    status read cmp_fails directly.  A self-check that did not pass is a failure the count shows.  */
253: 	if (cmp_fails > failures)
254: 		failures = cmp_fails;
255: 	if (!sc_g && failures == 0)
256: 		failures = 1;
257: 	printf("\n%d rows, %d failures\n", rows, failures);
258: 	if (failures == 0 && cmp_fails == 0 && sc_g)
259: 		printf("WDC_IDENTIFY_PASS\n");
260: 	else
261: 		printf("WDC_IDENTIFY_FAIL\n");
262: 	return (failures || cmp_fails || !sc_g) ? 1 : 0;
263: }
264: ```
