1311: #  reproduction is regress/fbpending_drain_probe.py (rung 3) and it is NOT run here --
1312: #  gate 14 (gate_arm.sh) runs it on all four timers, since #548.
1313: #
1314: #  BOTH SHIP BECAUSE NEITHER ALONE IS ENOUGH -- measured, not assumed:
1315: #    * the rung-3 probe cannot reach the boundary.  The core delivers at most
1316: #      TIMER_MAX_CATCHUP * TIMER_BASE_FREQUENCY = 68,157,440 increments per wall second, so
1317: #      2^31 of them take 31.5 s AT BEST and a gate row cannot spend that.  This harness does
1318: #      2^31 direct increments in ~4 s.
1319: #    * a mutant deleting the absolute ceiling (leaving the bound at the timer's own rate)
1320: #      PASSES the rung-3 probe on every timer and is caught only here, at emulated_hz above
1321: #      68 MHz -- reachable through the documented -I flag.
